# scripts/guards/check-checker-entrypoints.baseline
#
# Plan 262 Ф.А.1-bis (registry №531). Files that call `check_module(` /
# `check_module_with_sig_table(` / `check_module_with_expr_types(` /
# `check_module_with_expr_types_ide(` directly WITHOUT also calling
# `check_pipeline::prepare_module_for_check[_with]` in the same file —
# accepted as of this plan, for the reason next to each. A file NOT in this
# list that starts doing the same thing is a NEW unguarded direct call and
# reds the gate (that is the whole point of the guard).
#
# This is a RATCHET, not a design goal: every line here is a candidate for
# being wired into prepare_module_for_check by a later window, not a
# permanent exemption. Removing a line because the file now calls
# prepare_module_for_check is always welcome and never breaks this guard.
#
# format: one path per line, relative to repo root, forward slashes.

# Legacy/orphan binary (`nova-codegen`, built from compiler-codegen/Cargo.toml's
# own [[bin]]) — parallel to nova-cli's `nova`, but does not even call
# resolve_imports_inline at all today (see cmd_check/cmd_compile in this
# file), so it is not "missing prepare_module_for_check" so much as "missing
# import resolution entirely" — a pre-existing, larger gap than this plan's
# scope. Its only known live consumer is scripts/tools/setup_worktree_p118.sh
# (a historical, single-plan setup script). Flagged for the owner to decide:
# wire it up, or retire it — not decided by this window.
compiler-codegen/src/main.rs

# Doc-test / doc-render probes: `let _ = check_module(&module)` used only to
# trigger the checker's annotation side-effects for doc-rendering purposes
# (inferred types shown in generated docs), never to produce user-facing
# diagnostics. A wrong/missing import here degrades doc-rendering fidelity,
# not correctness — different risk class than registry #531's LSP false-red.
compiler-codegen/src/doc/watch_cache.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_allow_transit.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_expect_output.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_extern_links.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_golden.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_handler_matrix.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_handler_matrix_workspace.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_html_multipage.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_html_render.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_mcp.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_mutation.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_mutation_exec.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_mutation_workspace.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_newtype.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_perf.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_query.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_render_expr.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_source_url.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_warnings.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/doc_workspace_determinism.rs

# Unit tests of the checker itself (e.g. strict-effects flag behavior, a
# specific raw-effect-op diagnostic) — deliberately single-file, no imports
# to resolve, testing check_module's own logic rather than simulating a real
# entry point's pipeline.
compiler-codegen/tests/p131_raw_effect_op_enforce.rs
compiler-codegen/tests/strict_effects_flag.rs

# Performance benchmarks (`nova bench`) — measure the type-checker's own
# wall-clock cost on an already-prepared module; not a diagnostics-producing
# entry point a user sees, and re-routing it through prepare_module_for_check
# would fold unrelated pass costs into what the benchmark is trying to
# isolate.
nova-cli/src/bench/field_cache_wallclock.rs
nova-cli/src/bench/run.rs

# nova-lsp field-cache IDE decoration heuristics (semantic-token "cached"
# modifier, code lenses, pure-annotation code actions): five near-identical
# best-effort passes, each on a FRESH single-file parse with NO cross-file
# import resolution at all (deliberate — this is a fast local heuristic, not
# a diagnostics path). On any check_module failure they degrade to "no
# decoration" (return None / empty), never surfaced to the user as an error.
# Missing imports/embeds here means missed decoration, not false-red —
# different risk class than registry #531. The five copies are themselves a
# duplication worth extracting into one shared helper, but that is a
# separate cleanup from this plan's diagnostic-parity fix.
nova-lsp/src/semantic_tokens.rs
nova-lsp/src/server.rs
